  "id": "Compound::DB00115 - Gene::25974",
  "verbalization": "Cyanocobalamin appears to interact with Mmachc through a shared pathway involving Cobalamin Binding. The evidence suggests that Cyanocobalamin binds to Tcn2 or Tcn1, which in turn participate in Cobalamin Binding, and this process is recognized by Mmachc. This indicates that Mmachc is involved in the functional context of Cobalamin Binding, which is a critical step in the biochemical process of cobalamin metabolism. The high scores in all three paths suggest a consistent relationship, with Cyanocobalamin acting as a ligand that influences the activity of Tcn proteins, which in turn affect Mmachc. The overlapping mechanisms of Cobalamin Binding across different binding partners imply that Mmachc may be a key player in the regulation of cobalamin-related pathways, possibly through its involvement in the structural or functional context of these interactions.",
